# Cyrillic Alphabet | Math Greek Letter Symbols Rules
# [AUTHOR]: Carlos González Sanz
#
# [NOTE]: This file is part of the "Logic + Math Symbols" Dead Key,
# which has been separated to  better maintain
# different aspects pertaining to this extensive dead key.
#
# [NOTE]: The specific formatting of each character
# is determined by the following Perl-like pseudo-regular expression
# applied to a LaTeX keyword (\{}):
#
# > regexp(dead_greek(Cyrillic)) = \\с?{<dead_greek>[а-яА-Я]}?[\*_]?\с
#
# Where:
#   -> "с"              = Sans-serif
#   -> {[а-яА-Я]}       = Any alphabetical Cyrillic character enclosed in curly braces (preceded by <dead_greek>)
#   -> "*"              = Final Bold (inspired by Markdown)
#   -> "_"              = Final Italic (inspired by Markdown)
#
# All of these rules must be preceded by the <dead_greek> keysym after the first left curly brace
# (with the exception of the nabla operator (which is instead enclosed as {[Дд]_})
# and the Greek letter variables (which are of the form {<dead_greek>[а-яА-Я]_})
# inside the aforementioned regular expression).
#
# [Main source]: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_Alphanumeric_Symbols
#

